    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15108" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eclīpsis</span></b> , is,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκλειψις</span> (a
		forsaking, being absent): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis,</span>”
				<i>an eclipse of the sun</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 3, 22, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lunae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 4, 14</span></i>
			; and without <i>gen.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 12,
				9, § 53</span></i> (pure Lat. defectio and defectus). </div>
